Now the requirements again, you can give whatever the requirements needed as per the website that you want to build.

538
00:47:10,064 --> 00:47:16,644
完成修复后，提供已识别问题、已修复问题、测试表现以及剩余问题。
After completing the fixes, provide issued identity, issued fixed, test performance, and remaining issues.

539
00:47:17,024 --> 00:47:25,508
在给出提示词后，它会修复大部分问题，然后你可以用同样的提示词——比如你是一名 UX analyst
And after the prompt is given, it will fix most of the issues and you can test it again with the same prompt saying you are a UX analyst

540
00:47:25,934 --> 00:47:29,476
或者任何其他类型的工程师——来再次审阅网站。
or any other type of engineer to review the website.

541
00:47:29,966 --> 00:47:32,464
现在，构建者正在接收来自审核者的反馈。
Now the builder is receiving feedback from the reviewer.

542
00:47:32,974 --> 00:47:37,572
它将去执行这些改进，而不仅仅是简单地描述它们。
It's going to implement those improvements rather than just simply describing it.

543
00:47:38,094 --> 00:47:44,996
对更新后的应用进行第二次审查。对比当前的实现与预览中发现的问题。
Perform a second review of the updated applications. Compare current implementation against the issue identified in the preview.

544
00:47:45,454 --> 00:47:50,020
针对之前出现的每个问题，将其分类为已修复、部分修复和未修复。
For each previous issue, classify it as fixed, partially fixed, and not fixed.

545
00:47:50,544 --> 00:47:53,252
识别在更改中引入的任何新问题。
Identify any new problems introduced in the changes.

546
00:47:53,870 --> 00:47:55,812
先不要修改任何应用。
Do not modify any applications yet.

547
00:47:56,144 --> 00:47:58,500
而且我们不需要盲目信任第一次修复的结果。
And we don't have to trust the first fix.

548
00:47:58,704 --> 00:48:03,428
我们可以反复评估更新后的结果，直到问题彻底解决为止。
We can evaluate the updated result again and again until the result is fixed.

549
00:48:04,046 --> 00:48:11,108
现在，这个循环就是：构建、审查、修复、再次审查、再次修复，最后进行测试。
Now, the loop of building, reviewing, and fixing and reviewing again, fixing again, and then finally testing.

550
00:48:11,534 --> 00:48:15,972
从技术上讲，我们目前所做的一切都可以由一个智能体来完成。
Everything we have done so far could technically be performed by one agent.

551
00:48:16,224 --> 00:48:20,548
但想象一下，如果我们把这些职责分配给多个专门的智能体。
But imagine we split these responsibilities across multiple specialized agents.

552
00:48:20,944 --> 00:48:30,180
一个智能体负责调研，另一个编写代码，另一个进行测试，还有一个负责安全审查，而一个编排系统来协调它们所有。
One agent could do research, another could write the code, another could test it, another could perform the security review, and an orchestra could coordinate all of them.

553
00:48:30,606 --> 00:48:37,744
调研智能体再次产出结果，开发智能体利用这些结果，测试智能体检查实现情况，
The research again produces its findings, the development agent uses those findings, the testing agent checks the implementation,

554
00:48:37,824 --> 00:48:42,116
审核者识别问题，而编排系统将所有环节整合在一起。
the reviewer identifies the problem, and the orchestra brings everything together.

555
00:48:42,384 --> 00:48:45,348
这就是多智能体协同的基础。
This is the foundation of multi-agent orchestration.

556
00:48:45,744 --> 00:48:49,940
这也是传统AI辅助与智能体AI之间的核心区别。
And that's the key difference between traditional AI assistance and agentic AI.

557
00:48:50,300 --> 00:48:56,324
我们不再只是向AI索要答案，而是给AI一个目标，并让它去执行整个流程。
We're no longer just asking AI for an answer. We are giving AI a goal and allowing it to work through a process.

558
00:48:56,686 --> 00:49:01,412
它可以调研、规划、使用工具、创作、测试、评估，还能不断迭代。
It can research, plan, use tools, create, test, evaluate, and also iterate.

559
00:49:01,664 --> 00:49:12,144
当多个专门的智能体协同工作时，就能实现更复杂的流程。我们首先从了解智能体AI与传统AI系统有何不同开始。
And when multiple specialized agents are coordinated together, much more complex workflows becomes possible. We started by understanding what makes agent DKI different from traditional AI systems.

560
00:49:12,304 --> 00:49:19,140
我们探讨了智能体如何感知信息、思考问题，以及如何使用工具并执行操作。
We explored how agents perceive information, reason through problems, and also use tools and also execute the actions.

561
00:49:19,344 --> 00:49:29,444
我们也看到AI智能体如何调研信息、构建应用、遵循项目指令、审查自己的输出，并通过反馈循环不断改进。
We also saw how AI agents can research information, build applications follow project instructions, review their own output, and also continuously improve through feedback loops.

562
00:49:29,664 --> 00:49:30,980
最大的转变就在于此。
The biggest shift is this.

563
00:49:31,344 --> 00:49:34,564
我们不再仅仅是要求AI提供答案。
We are no longer just asking AI to provide answers.

564
00:49:34,894 --> 00:49:41,604
我们给AI设定目标，并让它通过一个包含规划、行动、评估和改进的流程来工作。
We are giving AI goals and allowing it to work through a process to plan, act, evaluate, and also to improve.

565
00:49:41,824 --> 00:49:49,104
当多个专门的智能体协同工作时，我们就开启了解决更大、更复杂问题的可能性。
And when multiple specialized agents work together, we unlock the possibility of solving much larger and more complex problems.

566
00:49:49,454 --> 00:49:55,812
智能体AI不仅仅是更聪明的对话，而是构建能够执行有意义操作的AI系统。
Agentic AI is not just about smarter conversations, it is about building AI systems that can make meaningful actions.

